{
  "_comment": "Shared end-to-end search match/filter vectors: raw query strings plus recipe documents in, matched recipe ids in final display order out. Consumed by tests/test_search_match_filter_vectors.py (which replays the corpus through the real API and database, timestamps included) and by SearchMatchFilterSharedVectorTests on iOS (which replays it through the Swift local-search pipeline). ingredient_match_text is the PostgreSQL jsonb-to-text rendering of the stored ingredients — generated by the database itself, never hand-written — and is the exact haystack bare-text tokens match against. Expected orders never depend on recipe-id tie-breaks (server ids are random UUIDs); score ties are resolved by distinct updated_at values instead. sort_by/sort_dir omitted means server defaults (relevance with text terms, updated_at desc without).",
